.TH BLAWG 1
.SH NAME
blawg \- an opinionated static site generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blawg
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blawg
builds a static site from a series of blog posts saved as
.I markdown
files with a
.I YAML
frontmatter containing post metadata, much as is used by
.B pandoc(1)
separated from the body of the post by three dashes
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Here is an example of a blog file:

.nf
.RS
title: Blawg
date: 2016\-10\-15 23:24:01
tags:
  \- unix
  \- vim
published: true
\-\-\-

# Blawg

Today I started to write my blawg...
.RE
.fi
.SH FRONTMATTER
The keys understood in a post's YAML frontmatter block:
.TP
.B title
Post title. Rendered through the same markdown/YAML title handling as the
body, so inline markdown (e.g. italics) is allowed.
.TP
.B date
Required. Must be in the form
.I YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM:SS,
e.g.
.I 2016\-10\-15 23:24:01.
Determines the post's URL path and its ordering against other posts.
.TP
.B published
Boolean, defaults to
.I false.
Unpublished posts are skipped entirely by
.B blawg
(excluded from the site, index, homepage, and RSS feed). Not used for
drafts, which are always written regardless of this key.
.TP
.B tags
A YAML list of strings. Rendered as the post's RSS category.
.TP
.B description
Free text, used as the post's RSS item description.
.TP
.B layout
Accepted for compatibility with other static site generators'
frontmatter, but currently unused by
.B blawg.
.TP
.B series
The series (chapter group) this post belongs to. The name doubles as
both the series' display title and the key used to group its posts
together \- see
.B SERIES
below.
.TP
.B part
The 1\-based chapter number within
.I series.
Required if
.I series
is set.
.SH SERIES
Posts sharing a
.I series
name are grouped into an ordered, multi\-part chapter list, ordered by
.I part.
Every post in a series has its full, part\-ordered chapter list available
to templates. Two posts in the same series may not share a
.I part
number, and a post with
.I series
set must also set
.I part;
both are build errors. If the template set defines a
.I series-index
block, each series additionally gets an index page at
.I /series/<slug>/.
.SH TEMPLATES
Templates are standard Go
.I html/template
files, loaded from the templates directory and referenced by
.I {{define "name"}}...{{end}}
block name. The following block names are looked up by
.B blawg;
all but
.I post,
.I index
and
.I page
are optional \- skipped if undefined.
.TP
.B post
Rendered once per post. Data is a
.I PostPage:
.I .Post
(the current post, see below) and
.I .PostList
(all published posts, a
.I Posts
slice, newest first).
.TP
.B index
Rendered at
.I /posts/.
Data is a
.I Posts
slice of all published posts.
.TP
.B page
Rendered once per page (from the pages directory). Data is a
.I *Page:
.I .Title,
.I .TitleText,
.I .Body,
.I .Path.
.TP
.B draft
Rendered once per draft. Data is a
.I DraftPage:
.I .Draft
(see below).
.TP
.B drafts\-index
Rendered at
.I /drafts/.
Data is a
.I []Draft
slice.
.TP
.B series\-index
Rendered at
.I /series/<slug>/
for each series. Data is a
.I Series:
.I .Name
(the series' display title) and
.I .Posts
(its chapters, a
.I Posts
slice ordered by
.I part).
.PP
A post or draft's own fields (available as
.I .Post
/
.I .Draft,
or directly when a sub\-template is invoked with one, as the bundled
example templates'
.I article
block does):
.TP
.B .Title / .TitleText
Rendered HTML title, and its plain\-text form.
.TP
.B .Date
A Go
.I time.Time.
.TP
.B .Body
Rendered post body, as HTML.
.TP
.B .Path
URL\-safe path to the post/draft, e.g.
.I 2016/10/15/blawg/
for a post,
.I drafts/blawg/
for a draft.
.TP
.B .Series / .Part
The frontmatter values, verbatim (empty string / zero if not in a series).
.TP
.B .SeriesPosts
This post's full chapter list (a
.I Posts
slice, ordered by
.I part),
or
.I nil
if not in a series. Each element has the same fields as above, including
its own
.I .Part,
so templates can find the current chapter by comparing
.I .Part
against the outer post's.
.TP
.B .SeriesPath
URL\-safe path to this post's series index page, e.g.
.I series/my\-deep\-dive/.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Fenced code blocks marked
.I mermaid
are rendered to inline SVG using
.B mmdc(1)
from
.I @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli,
which in turn requires a Chrome/Chromium binary available to Puppeteer.
If
.B mmdc
is not installed or fails, the block falls back to a plain
.I <pre><code>
block.

Install with:
.nf
.RS
npm install -g @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli
npx puppeteer browsers install chrome-headless-shell
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
pandoc(1), mmdc(1)